Template: bird-manager/append-managed-include
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Add the bird-manager include to /etc/bird/bird.conf?
  bird-manager found an external BIRD configuration that does not reference
  /etc/bird/live. Existing content will be preserved and a marked include of
  /etc/bird/live/bird-manager.conf will be appended.
  .
  If you choose "Yes", the current file is backed up as
  /etc/bird/bird.conf.bak-before-managed-entrypoint before the validated change.
  If you choose "No", bird-manager will not modify the main configuration and
  Apply will remain disabled until an administrator completes the migration.

Template: bird-manager/remove-all-data
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Remove all bird-manager data and generated BIRD configuration?
  If you choose "Yes", the package removes its SQLite database, staged files,
  backups, manifest, /etc/bird-manager/.env, its dedicated system account and
  the generated files in /etc/bird/live.
  .
  Before live files are removed, the current bird-manager include block in
  /etc/bird/bird.conf is replaced inline with the effective generated BIRD
  configuration. The candidate is validated with "bird -p" and reloaded with
  "birdc configure" when BIRD is active. No persistent backup copy of
  bird.conf is created. Unknown files in /etc/bird/live are preserved.
  .
  If you choose "No", the database, environment file and live configuration
  remain on disk for a later reinstall. "apt purge" always performs the full
  cleanup without asking this question.
